+# Agent Note: Durable context selection
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-17-durable-context-selection.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Provider-native encrypted context cannot be interpreted by unrelated models. Replacing the shared conversation surface with one provider's checkpoint destroys the input needed for a later route switch. Model requests must remain reconstructable from the session log.
+
+## Decision
+
+An effect-owned agent context provider selects messages after admission and before request freeze. The loop logs the selected projection and requires persistence before dispatch, then rechecks cancellation, ownership and source history. Ordinary requests retain their surface derivation; removing the owner logs a projection reset. Automatic basic compaction defers to an active owner. Manual compaction retains its explicit surface behavior.
+
+The session log stores auxiliary compaction input and completed output, complete checkpoint candidates, commit references and request projections as additive required event types. A selector publishes a commit only after candidate durability. The loop persists the commit together with its request projection before model dispatch. An uncommitted candidate is never selected. A later dispatch failure does not invalidate a completed checkpoint. Original surface history remains available independently of both native and portable checkpoints.
+
+Prepared adapters expose versioned native encoding, counting and compaction operations. A native prefix includes format and compatibility scope, and the LLM runtime rejects mismatches before adapter dispatch. Counting opaque data is the adapter's responsibility; its serialized byte length is not a token budget. The plugin chooses independent per-route policies and budgets without changing frozen requests.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Replace the original surface with an opaque checkpoint.** Foreign models cannot reconstruct the replaced conversation. Independent log-only checkpoints preserve both route-specific state and original messages.
+
+**Rewrite a request in stream middleware.** The request would diverge from the logged selection. Selection belongs before the loop's durable freeze boundary.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Checkpoint selection requires a persistence listener and records full selected windows, increasing log size. Old readers that do not know these required events cannot safely resume the session; additive event vocabulary does not provide downgrade support. Native counting and compaction availability are explicit adapter capabilities, and their absence fails selection without deleting history.
